Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. By 4 October the desk had
**412 reports** (the export repeats 15 rows; counted once by id). They were merged into #4471 as
one parser bug. They are two problems.

<Callout>
Not one issue. #4471 holds two problems, and only the first is the parser.
</Callout>

## The two problems

| # | Problem | Reports | Status |
|---|---------|--------:|--------|
| 1 | The shared parser reads dates month first; day-first tenants get flipped dates | 379 | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| 2 | The booking-v3 form hint prints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants (copper.studio, alder.physio, pale.harbour) | 33 | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |

379 + 33 = 412. Footnote: 5 of the 379 (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) read as a one-day move, not a month flip; they are filed under `parser` by tenant. Intake tagged 23 of the `parser` group as `hint` and 15 of the `hint` group as `parser`: the tag is a guess, the tenant is the evidence.

